# Spark (Readdle) — Vendor Security Review: Risk Acceptance Assessment

**Date:** 2026-06-18 · **Owner:** Kalle Hansson · **Verdict: KEEP — accept the risk. Effort is small.**

## TL;DR
Spark can be enabled via Normain's **documented risk-acceptance (exception) path**. Readdle/Spark holds **no SOC 2 / ISO 27001** of its own (only its Google Cloud infra is certified) — that is the one missing item. The Third-Party Management Policy explicitly covers "required documentation missing": accept alternate evidence + compensating controls + logged exception signed off by the Security Delegate. Same lightweight route already used for risk R-14 (~1-page memo + Vanta entry + calendar reminder). **The EU→US data-transfer point is closeable without moving servers** (see below). **Switching email clients is not warranted** — compliance work is roughly half a day.

